new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null	(date 1792175220642)
+++ b/docs/Query1-Contract.md	(date 1792175220642)
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Query 1 contract: missed visits by month
+
+Version 1.0, 2026-10-16. Owner: Jason. Story: OLAP-1. Query: Query 1 in [OLAP_Queries.md](OLAP_Queries.md).
+
+Amal's procedure, Cadan's endpoint and Leon's Postman tests all build against this file. Any change to it needs a PR and a post in #dev.
+
+## Procedure (Amal)
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Name | `dbo.usp_MissedVisitsByMonth` |
+| Parameters | None. Covers all agencies and all months. |
+| Source | OLAP warehouse (FactVisit and DimDate). Internals are up to Amal as long as the output matches this file. |
+| Sort | `Month` ascending |
+
+| Column | SQL type | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Month` | `char(7)` | Month of ScheduledStart (UTC), formatted `YYYY-MM` |
+| `VisitCount` | `int` | Visits in the month, excluding cancelled and not yet due |
+| `MissedCount` | `int` | Visits counted in `VisitCount` that are Missed |
+| `MissedPercent` | `decimal(5,1)` | `MissedCount * 100.0 / VisitCount`, rounded to 1 decimal place with `ROUND` |
+
+## Endpoint (Cadan)
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Method and path | `GET /api/reports/missed-visits-by-month` |
+| Request | No parameters, no body |
+| Success | `200 OK`, `Content-Type: application/json`, a JSON array of rows |
+| No data | `200 OK` with `[]` |
+| Database unavailable or query fails | `500` with the ASP.NET Core default problem details body |
+
+| JSON field | Type | From column |
+|---|---|---|
+| `month` | string, `YYYY-MM` | `Month` |
+| `visitCount` | integer | `VisitCount` |
+| `missedCount` | integer | `MissedCount` |
+| `missedPercent` | number, 1 decimal place | `MissedPercent` |
+
+Field names are camelCase (the ASP.NET Core default). The API returns no other fields. The chart works out Success as `visitCount - missedCount` (OLAP-1).
+
+## Rules
+
+These follow the Definitions table in [OLAP_Queries.md](OLAP_Queries.md).
+
+| Term | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| Missed | No check-in within 60 minutes of ScheduledStart (60 minutes counts as within), once ScheduledStart + 60 minutes has passed, and not Cancelled. A check-in after 60 minutes does not clear it. |
+| Missed source | Computed from ScheduledStart and ActualCheckIn only. Visit.Status is never Missed. |
+| Cancelled | Status = Cancelled. Excluded from both counts. |
+| Not yet due | ScheduledStart + 60 minutes has not passed. Excluded from both counts. |
+| Months with no counted visits | Left out of the result |
+| Time | All times are UTC; cutoffs compare exact timestamps to the second |
+
+## Worked example
+
+Sample visits, with the query run on 2026-10-16:
+
+| VisitID | ScheduledStart (UTC) | ActualCheckIn (UTC) | Status | Counted? | Missed? | Why |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | 2025-01-06 09:00:00 | 2025-01-06 09:05:00 | Completed | Yes | No | Checked in 5 minutes after start |
+| 2 | 2025-01-10 14:00:00 | 2025-01-10 15:00:00 | Completed | Yes | No | Exactly 60 minutes counts as within |
+| 3 | 2025-01-15 10:00:00 | none | Scheduled | Yes | Yes | No check-in |
+| 4 | 2025-01-20 11:00:00 | none | Cancelled | No | No | Cancelled |
+| 5 | 2025-02-03 09:00:00 | 2025-02-03 10:00:01 | Completed | Yes | Yes | Checked in 1 second after the cutoff |
+| 6 | 2025-02-12 13:00:00 | 2025-02-12 13:02:00 | Completed | Yes | No | Checked in 2 minutes after start |
+| 7 | 2025-02-20 08:00:00 | none | Scheduled | Yes | Yes | No check-in |
+| 8 | 2026-10-30 09:00:00 | none | Scheduled | No | No | Not yet due, so 2026-10 is left out |
+
+Procedure output:
+
+| Month | VisitCount | MissedCount | MissedPercent |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 2025-01 | 3 | 1 | 33.3 |
+| 2025-02 | 3 | 2 | 66.7 |
+
+Endpoint response:
+
+```json
+[
+  { "month": "2025-01", "visitCount": 3, "missedCount": 1, "missedPercent": 33.3 },
+  { "month": "2025-02", "visitCount": 3, "missedCount": 2, "missedPercent": 66.7 }
+]
+```
+
+## Sign-off
+
+- [ ] Shayan (analyst)
+- [ ] Amal (procedure)
+- [ ] Cadan (endpoint)
+- [ ] Leon (Postman tests)
